T65 -- 65xx compatible microprocessor core
------------------------------------------

Files:    rtl/t65/T65.vhd, rtl/t65/T65_Pack.vhd, rtl/t65/T65_ALU.vhd,
          rtl/t65/T65_MCode.vhd
Source:   FPGAARCADE SVN, T65.vhd rev 1347 (2015-05-27, "Ver 313");
          T65_ALU/MCode/Pack rev 1234 (2015-02-28); original at
          www.opencores.org. Provenance and file hashes: rtl/t65/SOURCE.md

MODIFIED by this project. Each change is marked "LOCAL PATCH" in the source
and kept as a patch in patches/ (apply in order, see patches/README.md):
  * 01: a taken branch reads PC+2, as the NMOS die does (ERRATA E-10); the
    JAM/KIL opcodes stop the CPU and hold the bus (E-11); ANE ($8B) uses the
    constant $EF, and $EE when RDY held its operand cycle (E-41); reset
    decrements S three times, sets I and leaves D unchanged (E-51); a
    default assignment in T65_ALU.vhd so the ALU synthesizes without a latch
  * 02: SHA/SHX/SHY/TAS write to the page of the stored value when the index
    crosses a page (ERRATA E-52)
  * 03: interrupts are polled on every RDY-held repeat of an instruction's
    last cycle and in a branch's operand cycle, as the die does (ERRATA
    E-39); an NMI that hijacks BRK/IRQ keeps its vector when RDY holds
    the vector read (E-53)
  * 04: when RDY holds the step before an SHA/SHX/SHY/TAS write, the value
    is stored without the "and (high byte + 1)" term, as the die does
    (ERRATA E-54)
T65_Pack.vhd and T65_MCode.vhd are as received.
The rest of this product -- including the 6510 wrapper rtl/cpu6510.v and the
board top rtl/top.v -- is original to this project and is not part of T65.
